        "original_id": "5678a1aa-bdda-5b89-9694-d2e9af69a284",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- TV Shows: Punchlines, Eye Guess, The Comedians, The Val Doonican Show\n- People: Bill Cullen, Paul Melba, Russ Abbot, Lennie Bennett, Stan Boardman, Jim Bowen, Jimmy Bright, Duggie Brown, Mike Burton, Jimmy Jones, Dave Butler, Brian Carroll, Frank Carson, Mike Coyne, Jimmy Cricket, Colin Crompton, Pauline Daniels, Charlie Daze, Vince Earl, Steve Faye, Eddie Flanagan, Stu Francis, Ken Goodwin, Jackie Hamilton, Jerry Harris, George King, Bobby Knutt, Bernard Manning, Mike McCabe, Mick Miller, Hal Nolan, Tom O'Connor, Tom Pepper, Bryn Phillips, Mike Reid, George Roper, Harry Scott, Sammy Thomas, Johnny Wager, Roy Walker, Charlie Williams, Lee Wilson, Lenny Windsor\n- Topics: game show hosting, nightclub comedians, working men's club comedians, television appearances\n\nFacts:\n- Eye Guess was an American game show that ran from 1966 to 1969.\n- In 1979, an American game show pilot titled Punchlines was produced as a failed pilot.\n- Bill Cullen hosted the failed 1979 American game show pilot Punchlines.\n- Punchlines was based on the failed 1979 American game show pilot Punchlines, which itself was a reboot of Eye Guess.\n- Bill Cullen hosted 23 shows over the course of his career and was nicknamed the Dean of Game Show Hosts.\n- Paul Melba made television appearances on Punchlines and on eight editions of The Val Doonican Show, in addition to appearing in clubs and theatres.\n- The Comedians gave a stage to nightclub and working men's club comedians of its era.\n- The comedians featured on The Comedians included Russ Abbot, Lennie Bennett, Stan Boardman, Jim Bowen, Jimmy Bright, Duggie Brown, Mike Burton, Jimmy Jones, Dave Butler, Brian Carroll, Frank Carson, Mike Coyne, Jimmy Cricket, Colin Crompton, Pauline Daniels, Charlie Daze, Vince Earl, Steve Faye, Eddie Flanagan, Stu Francis, Ken Goodwin, Jackie Hamilton, Jerry Harris, George King, Bobby Knutt, Bernard Manning, Mike McCabe, Paul Melba, Mick Miller, Hal Nolan, Tom O'Connor, Tom Pepper, Bryn Phillips, Mike Reid, George Roper, Harry Scott, Sammy Thomas, Johnny Wager, Roy Walker, Charlie Williams, Lee Wilson, and Lenny Windsor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
